  "method": "For each of 28 islands the GBIF occurrence API returned speciesKey and genusKey facet counts for Mammalia in the island box and in the mainland box, and the same for Chiroptera, Cetacea, Sirenia, Phocidae, Otariidae, Odobenidae and 12 domestic or commensal genera, which were subtracted; species with >= 3 records formed the sets. f = fraction of island species also present in the mainland set. Channel depth = greatest depth among 100 GEBCO 2020 points along the pre-registered straight transect (OpenTopoData API); width = transect length. Three islands with < 5 qualifying species (Pemba, Lombok, Cyprus) were dropped (n = 25). Spearman's rho between f and log depth, the partial Spearman correlation controlling log width, and the shallow (<= 120 m) vs deep (> 120 m) means were compared with the pre-registered thresholds.",
